<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<configuration>
    <!--
        Restore config for the smoke-restore consumer (nuget-packaging-plan.md §6 Phase 5).

        Deliberately separate from the repo-root nuget.config: this file must prove that a
        REAL external consumer's restore of Cs2DemoKit.* would succeed, which the repo-root
        config cannot do — its `local` source is mapped so broadly (CS2OpenDev.Sdk AND
        Cs2VideoGenerator.Core) that it would mask a broken Cs2DemoKit dependency graph, and it
        has no source for the freshly-packed nupkgs at all.

        Known-flaw fix encoded here (nuget-packaging-plan.md was going to clear + map only
        `Cs2DemoKit*` -> the smoke feed, which is incomplete): two Cs2DemoKit packages depend on
        CS2OpenDev packages that exist ONLY in the repo's committed local-packages/ feed, not on
        nuget.org — Cs2DemoKit.Analysis on CS2OpenDev.Sdk, and (since 2026-08-10) Cs2DemoKit.Parser
        on CS2OpenDev.Protos, which supplies the generated Valve message types the parser used to
        run protoc for. Without a source for them, restore 404s on dependencies that have nothing
        to do with what this smoke test is proving. So three sources, each mapped to exactly what
        it must supply:
          - nuget.org      -> everything unmapped (Google.Protobuf, YamlDotNet, M.E.Logging.*, …)
          - smoke feed     -> Cs2DemoKit* only (the packages under test)
          - repo local feed -> CS2OpenDev* only

        The CS2OpenDev mapping is NOT deletable-at-leisure any more. CS2OpenDev.Protos is a PUBLIC
        dependency of the published Cs2DemoKit.Parser (seven public members take its types), so a
        real external consumer restoring from nuget.org alone cannot succeed until CS2OpenDev.Protos
        is published there. That is the gate on the 1.0.0 nuget.org flip, not a smoke-test detail —
        owner decision 2026-08-10 is to flip both families together. Until then this mapping is what
        makes the smoke test representative of a consumer who has both feeds.

        Both non-nuget.org paths are relative to THIS file's directory (scripts/nuget-smoke/),
        matching the repo-root nuget.config's own convention of relative `local` paths. Override
        the smoke-feed location by pointing dotnet's "configfile" option at a copy of this file
        with a different `smoke` source value, or by populating the default path
        (../../artifacts/nuget-smoke-feed, i.e. repo-root/artifacts/nuget-smoke-feed) — nuget.yml
        and the local validation flow both do the latter.
    -->
    <packageSources>
        <clear/>
        <add key="nuget" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json"/>
        <add key="smoke" value="../../artifacts/nuget-smoke-feed"/>
        <add key="local" value="../../local-packages"/>
    </packageSources>
    <packageSourceMapping>
        <packageSource key="nuget">
            <package pattern="*"/>
        </packageSource>
        <packageSource key="smoke">
            <package pattern="Cs2DemoKit*"/>
        </packageSource>
        <packageSource key="local">
            <package pattern="CS2OpenDev*"/>
        </packageSource>
    </packageSourceMapping>
</configuration>
